{"record": "end", "run_id": "20261113T062748Z_dev-05_staged_ce77", "reason": "answered", "detail": "", "answer": {"answer": "The paper does not quote a detection significance for the GCE, either in σ or as a test statistic. Section 3.5 says the fitted GCE flux stays nonzero across all 80 diffuse-emission models. It adds that this \"alone does not establish its statistical significance.\" It also says the Δ(−2lnL) differences between the non-nested diffuse models cannot be read as squared Gaussian significances. The paper fits GCE spectra to dark matter models, and the best fits have χ²/dof of roughly 1.9–3.7. These measure goodness of fit, not detection significance. The TS definition in the paper is used only for catalog source masking.", "found": false, "evidence": [{"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "3.5"}, {"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "3.4"}, {"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "8"}]}, "turns": 10, "seconds": 20.498, "tool_calls": 12, "tool_result_chars": 73768, "input_tokens": 22, "output_tokens": 1505, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 27047, "cache_read_input_tokens": 186704, "parser_versions": ["4"], "response_models": ["claude-sonnet-5-5"], "ended_at": "2026-11-13T06:28:08+00:00"}
